📗
  🧬 A shape: what a body, a query or an answer is made of. It has a name,
  and fields that are declared with the calls a binder reads with:

    🆕🧬 🔤NewTodo🔤❗️ ➡️ newTodo
    🔡 newTodo 🔤title🔤 1 200❗️                 💭 a text of 1 to 200 characters
    👌🔸🍬 newTodo 🔤done🔤❗️                    💭 a boolean that may be missing
    💬 newTodo 🔤title🔤 🔤What is to be done🔤❗️  💭 for the document

  A route is told that a shape is its body (🌸 route shape❗️) or its query
  (🔎 route shape❗️). A binder then reads by it (🌸🔸🧬 input❗️), and the
  app's OpenAPI document describes it. So a bound is written once. Every
  call that adds to a shape returns the shape. Make shapes before 🚀: they
  are only read once the server runs.
