  🧬🔸📥 What a binder read by a shape: the fields by their names, each asked for
  as the kind it is.

    🌸🔸🧬 input❗️ ➡️ read
    🔡 read 🔤title🔤❗️           💭 the text
    👌🔸🍬 read 🔤done🔤❗️         💭 the boolean, or no value when it was not sent

  A field that has to be there and was wrong is what its reader gives then:
  the empty text, the low bound, 👎, the first of the choices. So a handler
  asks the binder whether anything was wrong (🚩 input❗️) before it uses
  what was read. A choice is a text. A field that the shape does not have,
  and one asked for as another kind than it is, is the empty text, 0, 0.0,
  👎, or no value.
